Ashly,

I do not know whether these can be combined in Slicer, but they can be combined in R (many ways to do so in fact). One option is to use the ‘combine.subsets’ function in geomorph (read the help file for proper implementation!).  Another option is to treat each as a 2D matrix (rows = specimens columns = coordinates), append them column-wise, and convert to a 3D array.

